findings.claim:
Pre-existing Sim.Ui collision, NOT introduced by lane U (Sim.Ui is unchanged since 1601c74), found while measuring. At 1080×640 with a section open and the Age panel open:
- the OVERLAYS tab overlaps the LEGEND tab;
- the OVERLAYS tab runs 10 px past the map's right margin;
- a click on the OVERLAYS control toggles the legend instead, so the overlay controls cannot be unfolded by click in that state.

Why it matters to the proposal: §3's inventory ('MEASURED by reading') places the two tabs in separate corners and never mentions this. E7 requires the rail to avoid both tabs 'at … the narrow 1080 × 640 window, with the context column open …, the overlays folded and unfolded, the Age panel open'. In that state the existing controls already collide, so the premise that 'the existing legend and overlay rows still pass' does not cover it. The existing placement bar also overlaps the Age panel there (U2-1). The Sim.Ui defect needs routing to the queue; the proposal should name the state rather than promise non-overlap in it.

